<task id="040" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Job C — email-triggered tasks/events via the shipped create-task pattern (`CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event`), cited</title>
    <phase>P4 — Job C + intent</phase>
    <gate>after:020,022</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <tags>bff-api, catalog</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates records (tasks/events) from email content on the AI-directed create path; deadline-bearing entries require human confirm (NFR-06 / ADR-015); citation to the source communication is load-bearing. Reuses the shipped `CREATE-TASK@v1` pattern — MUST NOT fork a second create mechanism. BFF-touching (catalog data + Ai via PublicContracts): publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Reuses a fully shipped, well-specified pattern (`CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record`); the work is wiring the email trigger + citation + confirm gate onto an existing capability, not novel design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares the Job C create path + `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams with 041 (which grounds on this path); serialize. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>020, 022</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement **Job C** (FR-14): email content triggers tasks/events via the **shipped create-task pattern** — `CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event` — on the record the email is associated to (020), **cited to the source communication**. Reuse the shipped capability end-to-end; do NOT fork a second task-creation mechanism.

    Reach AI + the create tool **only** through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (ADR-013 facade) as a **code-directed Action + Binding** (ADR-039). MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph playbook engine. The create is a **gated** `dataverse.create_record` — deadline-bearing entries (anything with a due/deadline date) require **human confirm** (NFR-06 / ADR-015); nothing deadline-bearing auto-finalizes.

    Ground the trigger in the triage signal already produced on the enrichment path (022) — do not run a second full LLM pass. Every created task/event carries a citation to the source communication (email + locator) and lands on the correct associated record. **NFR-04:** Job C is best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send path.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication + Ai domains, authoritative on the shipped `create-task` capability (`CREATE-TASK@v1`), the gated `dataverse.create_record` tool, the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade (ADR-013), Action + Binding authoring (ADR-039), the `TaskActionCore` write core, and NFR-06 / ADR-015 (deadline-bearing → confirm). Fluent in `docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Given an email associated to a record (020) with a triage signal (022) implying a task/event, Job C creates the task/event on the right record via `CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event`, cited to the source communication. A deadline-bearing entry requires human confirm before finalizing. The capability reuses the shipped create-task pattern (no fork), reaches AI only via `PublicContracts`, and is best-effort on the enrichment path. Build clean; unit + seam tests + a golden-utterance eval case pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      r1 turns email into action. Job C is the "email implies work" path: it reuses the shipped create-task capability rather than building a new one. The reference Binding + input schema exist (`infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json` + `infra/dataverse/inputschemas/create-task-v1.input.schema.json`); `TaskActionCore` is the write core; the create tool is gated `dataverse.create_record`. This task authors the email→create-task Action + Binding (catalog data) + wires the trigger onto the enrichment path.

      NFR-06 / ADR-015: deadline-bearing entries require confirm — a task with a due date is not auto-finalized. The citation to the source communication is what makes the created item defensible (why does this task exist? — because of email X). 041 grounds attachment-derived action extraction on this same create path.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs (REUSE — the create-task write core `CREATE-TASK@v1` fronts)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (REUSE — the facade seam to the create path)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/inputschemas/create-task-v1.input.schema.json (REUSE/MIRROR — the CREATE-TASK@v1 input schema; author the email→create Binding mirror-first)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (REFERENCE — Binding row shape for the create-task consumer)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (REFERENCE — enrichment path where the trigger fires best-effort, NFR-04)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs (REFERENCE — the triage signal to reuse; no 2nd full LLM pass)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md (Action + Binding authoring; the create-task worked example)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>020 (the association that supplies the target record), 022 (the triage signal that implies the task).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-14">Scope: email content triggers tasks/events via the shipped create-task pattern (`CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event`), cited to the source communication, on the correct associated record; deadline-bearing entries require confirm.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: code-directed Action + Binding via catalog data reusing the shipped create-task capability; MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine; MUST NOT fork a second task-creation mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-03">Scope: reach AI + the create tool ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` into Communication code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-015">Scope: deadline-bearing entries (with a due/deadline date) require human confirm; nothing deadline-bearing auto-finalizes; each created item carries a citation to the source communication.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04 / ADR-045">Scope: Job C is best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (reuses the shipped create-task capability + PublicContracts facade; catalog data, no new service); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + seam tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07 / ADR-039">Scope: the Job C Action/Binding adds a golden-utterance eval case (blocking merge gate).</constraint>
  </constraints>

