  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, `docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md` (create-task worked example), ADR-039, ADR-013, ADR-015 (deadline-bearing → confirm).</step>
    <step order="2">Read `TaskActionCore.cs`, `create-task-v1.input.schema.json`, `sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json`, and the enrichment path — identify the shipped create path, the input-schema shape to mirror, and where the trigger fires on enrichment.</step>
    <step order="3">Author the email→create-task Action + Binding (catalog data, mirror-first over the create-task input schema) that, given the associated record + reused triage signal (022), proposes/creates a task/event on the right record via `CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event`, cited.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the deadline-bearing confirm gate: an entry with a due/deadline date requires human confirm; non-deadline-bearing entries may auto-finalize per the shipped gate. Attach the source-communication citation.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire the trigger onto the enrichment path best-effort (NFR-04) — log + degrade on failure, never throw up capture/send.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the golden-utterance eval case (NFR-07). Write unit + seam tests: (a) an email implying a task creates one on the right record, cited to the source; (b) a deadline-bearing entry requires confirm (does not auto-finalize); (c) the create reuses `CREATE-TASK@v1` / gated `dataverse.create_record` (no forked mechanism, grep-verifiable); (d) a Job C failure does not fail the enrichment path (NFR-04). ADR-038 boundary mocks only.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus reuse-not-fork, deadline→confirm, citation, facade discipline, non-fatal); `adr-check` against ADR-039 / ADR-013 / ADR-015 + spec FR-14 / NFR-04 / NFR-06 / NFR-07. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + create path; coordinate with 041 which grounds on this path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (040 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (create-task Binding shape, confirm-gate wiring, citation approach) for 041.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the shipped `CREATE-TASK@v1` input schema / create path cannot express the email-triggered task/event without a schema change or a second create mechanism, STOP and surface per root §6 / §6.5 rather than forking a parallel task-creation path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The shipped `create-task` capability (`CREATE-TASK@v1` → gated `dataverse.create_record` → `sprk_event`) already creates tasks/events; `TaskActionCore` is the write core.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this is a new Action + Binding (catalog data) mirror-first over the shipped create-task input schema, reusing the shipped create path end-to-end; no new create mechanism, no new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without Job C, an email that implies work (a task/event) results in nothing — the "email into action" pillar (FR-14 / Success Criterion 7 grounding) does not ship, and 041's attachment-derived action extraction has no create path to ground on.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

